  "notes": "The Dutch trance-pop / bubblegum-Eurodance board — Sebastiaan Molijn and Eelke Kalberg working with Dennis van den Driesschen and Wessel van Diepen — the four names behind both the section's biggest trance-pop act and its biggest chant-hook party act. Alice Deejay and Vengaboys are in ARTISTS; this model is the room. What the board contributes that neither act states alone is the fill vocabulary: the party-side records substitute \"crowd/airhorn/whistle FX for drum fills\" while the trance-side records use \"long snare rolls instead\", so both live here — an impact/triangle lane alongside the tambourine and shaker, with the roll ladder on and a moderate ramp. The rest is the canonical Eurodance grammar the entry cites: kick on 1/5/9/13, clap layered on 2&4, open hats on the offbeat eighths, 16th tambourine or shaker. The identifying melodic parameter is theirs rather than either act's: \"a single sustained supersaw lead line that is the record's hook, stated before the vocal and restated as the drop — trance timbre applied to pop song-form\", which is a low-density legato lead over 8-bar loops with the hook stated in the intro. The bass is \"root-and-octave or offbeat-8th saw locked tight to the kick; simple by design so the saw lead has the whole midrange\" — a kick mirror at 0.96 with an octave as the only passing tone. Their production model is a studio project with a separated recorded voice and performing face. ⚠ The research marks the harmonic range `[LOW-CONF]` and says the tempo and all placements come from the Eurodance and trance conventions; both marks are repeated here, and every number above is INFERRED.",
